---
export const prerender = true;
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<Base title="Editorial &amp; Template Policy | WaiverMaker" description="How WaiverMaker creates, reviews, and describes its waiver templates.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal-page"><article class="legal-content">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' },
    ]} />
    <h1>Editorial &amp; Template Policy</h1>
    <h2>How our templates are created</h2><p>WaiverMaker templates are built by reviewing commonly used waiver provisions for each activity type, drawing on standard legal document structures used across the industry. Templates include provisions that are commonly relevant to that activity.</p>
    <h2>What "activity-specific" means</h2><p>Each activity type generates a document with clauses relevant to that activity's common risks and consent requirements: for example, a tattoo waiver includes bloodborne pathogen acknowledgement and aftercare responsibility; a rock climbing waiver includes equipment inspection and belayer competency clauses. "Activity-specific" refers to the clauses included, not to a determination that the document satisfies every legal requirement in any particular jurisdiction.</p>
    <h2>What "governing state" means</h2><p>When you select a state, WaiverMaker populates the governing-law section of your document with that state's name. This does not mean WaiverMaker has verified that the document satisfies all applicable laws, regulations, or requirements in that state. State laws affecting waiver enforceability vary significantly.</p>
    <h2>Template versioning</h2><p>Each template carries a version number and generation date. When templates are updated, the version number changes. We do not automatically update previously generated documents.</p>
    <h2>Review process</h2><p>Templates are reviewed periodically for accuracy and updated when we identify significant issues. The "Last reviewed" date on each page reflects when we last audited the content for accuracy. We do not update this date on a schedule: only when actual review occurs.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2><p>If you identify an error or concern in our content, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@waivermaker.com">support@waivermaker.com</a>. We take accuracy seriously and will review reported issues promptly.</p>
    <h2>What we don't guarantee</h2><ul><li>Is enforceable in your jurisdiction</li><li>Satisfies all applicable laws, regulations, or insurer requirements</li><li>Has been reviewed or approved by an attorney</li><li>Is appropriate for your specific situation</li></ul>
    <h2>Legal advice disclaimer</h2><p>Nothing on WaiverMaker.com constitutes legal advice. For advice specific to your business and jurisdiction, consult a licensed attorney.</p>
  </article></main>

  <!-- Generator CTA -->
  <div class="editorial-cta">
    <h2>Generate Your Free Waiver</h2>
    <p>The tool this policy describes — free, no account required.</p>
    <a href="/" class="cta-button">Generate My Waiver &rarr;</a>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .editorial-cta {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto 60px;
    padding: 36px 40px;
    background: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .editorial-cta h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .editorial-cta p {
    color: #475569;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #059669;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 15px;
    padding: 14px 28px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .cta-button:hover {
    background: #047857;
  }
</style>
